{"name":"Evil Forces","hex":"#770022","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Intending to harm; malevolent.","Morally corrupt."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Moral badness; wickedness; malevolence; the forces or behaviors that are the opposite or enemy of good.","Something which impairs the happiness of a being or deprives a being of any good; something which causes suffering of any kind to sentient beings; harm; injury; mischief."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil"},{"term":"forces","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of force"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Troops.","The orchestral instrumentation (and voices) used in a musical production."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forces"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evil","blocks":[{"text":"Evil, as a concept, is usually defined as profound immorality, and it is related to acts that cause pain and suffering to others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg/330px-Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evil"},{"title":"Force","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, a force is an action that can cause an object to change its velocity or its shape, or to resist other forces, or to cause changes of pressure in a fluid. In mechanics, force makes ideas like pushing or pulling mathematically precise. Because the magnitude and direction of a force are both important, force is a vector quantity. The SI unit of force is the newton (N), and force is often represented by the symbol F."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Force_examples.svg/330px-Force_examples.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https